        reading: [{ heading: "What you pass on", body: "Socrates said the unexamined life is not worth living. The parent version: an unexamined belief you pass to your child is not really yours to pass. You're handing on something you received without testing — and your child receives it the same way. The chain continues. The Socratic practice for parents: identify one belief you're transmitting — about success, about morality, about what matters — and ask: have I examined this? Do I believe it because it's true, or because it's familiar? If it survives examination, pass it on with confidence. If it doesn't, pass on the practice of examining it instead. The original WisdomForge booklet on Socrates is the longer text. This assist is for the parent who realizes they're living on borrowed beliefs and handing them down." }],
