        parentBriefing: "Democritus is the first materialist: everything is atoms moving in void. For this age: atoms are tiny building blocks too small to see. Everything is made of them — you, the screen, the air. The cool part: we know they're there because the reasoning works, even though we can't see them. That's philosophy — believing something you can't see because the argument holds.",
